<p>Decimal 60900. Read only.</p>
<p>A byte inside the kernal ROM that identifies which video standard the machine
was built for: it reads <strong>12 on a PAL VIC 20</strong> and <strong>5 on an
NTSC one</strong>.</p>
<p>The two machines differ in ways that matter to a game: PAL runs at 50 frames a
second with 312 raster lines, NTSC at 60 frames a second with 261, and the sound
pitches differ slightly. Testing this byte lets one program adjust its timing for
both.</p>
<p>It is a ROM address, so read it through an index rather than assigning it
directly.</p>

<p>Example</p>
<code>
if (PAL_OR_NTSC[0] = 12) then
	frameDelay := 8   // PAL, 50Hz
else
	frameDelay := 10; // NTSC, 60Hz
</code>
